      <section class="section-why_choose">
        <div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container-1280 v-padding-120 w-container">
          <div class="slider-wrapper gap-64">
            <div class="top_side-800">
              <div wb-component="smart-animate" class="gap-4-purpose">
                <div class="text-12-caps opacity-60">THE challenges</div>
                <h2 class="h1"><span class="span-pink-2">The challenges</span></h2>
              </div><img sizes="100vw" srcset="/images/Frame-1707478537_2Frame-1707478537.avif 500w, /images/Frame-1707478537_2.avif 2400w" alt="A purple background with squares and dots" src="/images/Frame-1707478537_2.avif" loading="lazy" class="image-why_shoose">
            </div>
            <div wb-component="smart-animate" class="wrapper-out max-100">
              <div class="left-out is-relative max-100">
                <div class="card-contaiiner">
                  <div class="card no-fill"><img src="/images/Frame-2147257699.avif" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" srcset="/images/Frame-2147257699-p-500.avif 500w, /images/Frame-2147257699-p-800.avif 800w, /images/Frame-2147257699.avif 1176w" alt="" class="img-100"></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="right-out max-100">
                <div class="gap-16">
                  <h3 class="text-32"><span class="span">Retention-specific campaign</span></h3>
                  <div class="text-16-150 color-white-80">Unlike awareness or acquisition campaigns, retention is not about introducing the product to the general public. It is about keeping existing customers engaged, informed, and confident that the product is still growing with their needs. For ClickUp, this meant the content had to support an ongoing relationship with users by helping them understand updates, adopt features, and see that ClickUp is listening to what they need.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div wb-component="smart-animate" class="wrapper-out max-100">
              <div class="right-out max-100">
                <div class="gap-16">
                  <h3 class="text-32"><span class="span">Strict brand guidelines</span></h3>
                  <div class="text-16-150 color-white-80">Brand consistency was key. As a well-established enterprise, ClickUp already had a strict design system, colour palette, and clear visual rules. The challenge was making sure every asset did not just look polished, but felt unmistakably ClickUp — from the layout and UI details to the transitions and animation style.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="left-out fill-content">
                <div class="card-contaiiner">
                  <div class="card no-fill"><img src="/images/brand-guideline-illustration.avif" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" srcset="/images/brand-guideline-illustration-p-500.avif 500w, /images/brand-guideline-illustration-p-800.avif 800w, /images/brand-guideline-illustration-p-1080.avif 1080w, /images/brand-guideline-illustration.avif 1176w" alt="" class="img-100"></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div wb-component="smart-animate" class="wrapper-out max-100">
              <div class="left-out is-relative max-100">
                <div class="card-contaiiner">
                  <div class="card no-fill"><img src="/images/kanban-grab-illustration.avif" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" srcset="/images/kanban-grab-illustration-p-500.avif 500w, /images/kanban-grab-illustration-p-800.avif 800w, /images/kanban-grab-illustration-p-1080.avif 1080w, /images/kanban-grab-illustration.avif 1176w" alt="" class="img-100"></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="right-out max-100">
                <div class="gap-16">
                  <h3 class="text-32"><span class="span">Communication and timeline management</span></h3>
                  <div class="text-16-150 color-white-80">Communication took a little more planning. Most of our team is based across the UK and Asia, while ClickUp’s team is in the US, which gave us a smaller window for real-time conversations each day. To keep projects moving, we had to ask clear questions early, confirm details upfront, and set realistic timelines when multiple tasks were running at once.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="line-gradient-2"></div>
      </section>
